module

public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.StableReduction.NumericalType.Basic
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Weight

/-!
# The numerical type of a regular model

Let `R` be a local ring of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, for instance a discrete valuation ring with a uniformizer, with residue field
`k`, and let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme, proper and flat over `R`, all of whose
points have codimension at most two and whose generic point lies away from the closed point, such
as a proper regular model of a curve over `R`. Write `Cᵢ` for the irreducible components of the
special fibre, with their reduced structures, and suppose that `H¹` of the structure sheaf of
every `Cᵢ` is finite-dimensional over `k` and that the special fibre is connected. Finiteness of
`H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` follows from properness.

Following [Stacks, Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Y), the special fibre
then defines a numerical type in the sense of
[Stacks, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z)
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`), with

* components the irreducible components `Cᵢ` of the special fibre;
* multiplicities `mᵢ`, the orders of vanishing of `π` along the `Cᵢ`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultiplicity`);
* weights `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k] = dim_k H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, where `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` is the constant
  field of `Cᵢ` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight`);
* genera `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, taken over the constant field;
* intersection matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`).

The axioms of a numerical type are the properties of these data proved in
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Matrix` and
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Weight`: the intersection matrix is symmetric with
nonnegative off-diagonal entries and kills the multiplicity vector, its graph is connected
because the special fibre is, and `wᵢ` divides its `i`-th row. The component set is nonempty by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.nonempty_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint`.

The combinatorial theory of `TauCeti.NumericalType`, such as its signed genus
`TauCeti.NumericalType.arithmeticGenus` and its weighted Picard group
`TauCeti.NumericalType.Pic`, thereby applies to regular models.

## Main declarations

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`: the numerical type of the special
  fibre of a regular model.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_weight`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_intersection` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_genus`: its data.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus`:
  `wᵢ gᵢ = dim_k H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, comparing the genus over the constant field with the genus
  over the residue field.

## Implementation notes

The definition is exposed so that its component type is, definitionally, the type of
codimension-one points of `X` in the special fibre that indexes
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`; the lemmas on its data are stated
for those points.

The `H¹` finiteness hypothesis is bundled in the structure
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.HasFiniteDimensionalSpecialFiberComponentTrivialCohomologyOne`, from
`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.SpecialFiber.Weight`, rather than passed to the
definition as a separate hypothesis. A hypothesis whose statement contains a proof term, here
the closedness of `closure {η}`, has that proof abstracted into an auxiliary lemma when it is a
binder of a definition, and the kernel then compares it, inside large cohomology types, with the
unabstracted statements of the lemmas it is passed to; the fields of a structure keep their
statements, and checking the definition stays fast.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Section 55.3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Y) and
  [Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Y).
* Q. Liu, *Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves*, Section 9.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Order
open TauCeti TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData (vanishingIdeal)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R))

variable [Ring.DimensionLEOne R] [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] [IsProper toBase] [Flat toBase]
  (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2) (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
  (hC : toBase.HasFiniteDimensionalSpecialFiberComponentTrivialCohomologyOne)
  {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)
  (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))

/-- **The numerical type of a regular model**
([Stacks, Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Y)). Let `X` be a regular
Noetherian integral scheme, proper and flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose
maximal ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two,
generic point away from the closed point and connected special fibre, and suppose that `H¹` of
the structure sheaf of every component of the special fibre is finite-dimensional over the
residue field `k`. Finiteness of `H⁰` follows from properness.

Its components are the irreducible components `Cᵢ` of the special fibre, with multiplicities the
orders `mᵢ` of `π` along them, weights `wᵢ = dim_k H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, genera
`gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` over the constant fields `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, and intersection
matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`. -/
@[expose]
def specialFiberNumericalType : NumericalType.{u} where
  Component := (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
    (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset
  componentDecidableEq := Classical.decEq _
  componentNonempty := by
    obtain ⟨η, hη'⟩ := toBase.nonempty_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint hη
    exact ⟨⟨η, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hη'⟩⟩
  multiplicity j := ⟨toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j,
    toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_pos hη (hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π)
      (toBase.ne_zero_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη hπ) j ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2)⟩
  weight i := ⟨toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2),
    toBase.specialFiberWeight_pos _
      (toBase.finiteDimensional_cohomology_zero_subscheme_closure_singleton
        ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))⟩
  intersection := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
  intersection_isSymm := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη
    (fun _ ↦ toBase.finiteDimensional_cohomology_zero_subscheme_closure_singleton)
    hC.finiteDimensional_one
  offDiagonal_nonneg _ _ := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_nonneg_of_ne hX hη
    (fun _ ↦ toBase.finiteDimensional_cohomology_zero_subscheme_closure_singleton)
    hC.finiteDimensional_one
  connected := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_reflTransGen hX hη
    (fun _ ↦ toBase.finiteDimensional_cohomology_zero_subscheme_closure_singleton)
    hC.finiteDimensional_one hconn
  fiber_relation i := by
    simpa [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, mul_comm] using congrFun
      (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_mulVec_specialFiberMultiplicity hX hη
        (fun _ ↦ toBase.finiteDimensional_cohomology_zero_subscheme_closure_singleton)
        hC.finiteDimensional_one hπ hreg) i
  weight_dvd i j := toBase.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j
  genus i := Module.finrank
    Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
    (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (vanishingIdeal
      ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1)

/-- The multiplicity of a component of the special fibre in the numerical type of a regular model
is the order of vanishing of `π` along it. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity
    (i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
      (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hC hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i :=
  (rfl)

/-- The weight of a component `C` of the special fibre in the numerical type of a regular model is
`dim_k H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)`, the degree of the constant field of `C` over the residue field `k`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight
    (i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
      (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hC hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The intersection matrix of the numerical type of a regular model is the intersection matrix of
its special fibre. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_intersection :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hC hπ hreg hconn).intersection =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη :=
  (rfl)

/-- The genus of a component `C` of the special fibre in the numerical type of a regular model is
`dim_κ H¹(C, 𝒪_C)` over the constant field `κ = H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` of `C`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_genus
    (i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
      (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hC hπ hreg hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank Γ((vanishingIdeal
          ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
        (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (vanishingIdeal
          ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  (rfl)

/-- **Weight times genus is the genus over the residue field.** For a component `C` of the special
fibre of a regular model, with weight `w = [κ : k]` and genus `g = dim_κ H¹(C, 𝒪_C)` over its
constant field `κ` in the numerical type, `w g = dim_k H¹(C, 𝒪_C)` over the residue field `k`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus
    (i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
      (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hC hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℕ) *
        (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hC hπ hreg hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (vanishingIdeal
        ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  toBase.specialFiberWeight_mul_finrank_cohomology_one _

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

end
